# {{format_name}} file format — implementation notes

`tmiki plugin new` wrote this file for the plugin `{{id}}`. It describes the
made-up "tmiki sample" format that the template reads, in the shape the notes
of a real format take.
Replace every section with what you find about your format, from which
sample files, and keep 9. "Open items" honest: PLUGIN_SPEC.md 8 asks for it.

All integer fields are little-endian.

## 1. Where the samples come from

| file | made by | what it shows |
|---|---|---|
| `tests/corpus/sample.{{ext}}` | `tmiki plugin new` | three layers: an opaque background, an offset half-opaque layer, a hidden layer |

## 2. File header

```
offset  size  field
────────────────────────────────────────────
0x00    8B    magic "TMISMPL1"
0x08    u32   canvas width
0x0C    u32   canvas height
0x10    u32   layer count
0x14    ...   layer records, bottom to top
```

## 3. Layer record

```
size  field
────────────────────────────────────────────
u16   name length N
N B   name, UTF-8
i32   x (left edge on the canvas)
i32   y (top edge on the canvas)
u8    flags: bit 0 = visible
u8    opacity, 0..255
u32   PNG length M
M B   the layer's pixels as a PNG (RGBA or any PNG the host reads)
```

The file ends right after the last record.

## 4. Layer tree

Flat: every layer is a raster layer at the top level.

## 5. Blend modes

None: every layer is drawn `normal`.

## 6. Composite

The file has no composite of its own; the plugin asks for
`render(generic-v1)`.

## 7. Write-back

A layer's PNG can be replaced: its record is written again with the new
PNG's length, every other byte is copied as it was.

## 8. Mapping to tmi:format

| file | WIT |
|---|---|
| layer record | `layer` (kind `raster`, `ready` bitmap: `image(png)` of the PNG's span) |
| record index | `stable-id` `layer-<index>` |
| opacity byte | `opacity` = byte / 255; `semantic` `opacity_byte` |

## 9. Open items

- (none for the sample format)
